//! The Simplicity programs an order spends by, pruned, as sequentia-contracts
//! publishes them: `templates/arca_order/fills.json` (`arca/order-2`, the fill
//! of a resting order in the tree) and `templates/seqdex_order/fills.json`
//! (`seqdex/order`, SeqDEX's order, which an `order-2` leaf lands as). Each
//! pruned program is one constant per path, whatever the order, so a spend is
//! built with no compiler. Copied byte for byte; the regtest tests spend each
//! one on the node.

/// The commitment root of `arca/order-2`.
pub const ORDER_CMR: &str = "fac4e5ebe8c377159c28f5fc74e6c492132983859d500081e46c727641b9e164";

/// The commitment root of `seqdex/order`.
pub const SEQDEX_ORDER_CMR: &str = "f9b42b838b6295f4f376760fbb02eed9cb20f872f07ee4b9df7273d26822ee44";

